Restore exact source-envelope bytes without invoking a native format codec.

Usage:
  cueson [global options] restore [options] INPUT.cueson.json

Options:
  -o, --output PATH  Restore one asset to a literal path.
  --output-dir DIR   Restore all assets beneath an existing directory.
  -f, --force        Replace approved existing regular files.
  --strict-metadata  Require every captured timestamp to be restored.
  --no-metadata      Skip timestamp restoration.

Global options:
  -q, --quiet  Suppress informational and success diagnostics.
  --silent     Suppress every non-error diagnostic.
  --no-color   Disable diagnostic color.
  -h, --help   Show help.
  --           End option processing; following paths and operands remain literal.

Notes:
  Multi-asset documents require --output-dir. Metadata modes are mutually exclusive.

Streams:
  stdout  Always empty.
  stderr  Metadata warnings and errors allowed by the global diagnostic filters.

Exit codes:
  0  Command or explicit help completed successfully; warnings may be present.
  1  An accepted operation failed during processing, cancellation, or runtime I/O.
  2  Command syntax, an operand, an option, or a pre-execution requirement was invalid.

Examples:
  cueson restore --output restored.srt document.cueson.json
  cueson restore --output-dir restored document.cueson.json
